{
  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2024_W48_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-48",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2024_W48_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-48.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2024-11-29",
  "report_week": "48",
  "report_period": "Week 48 (22nd Nov to 29th Nov 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Japanese owners committed their Newcastlemax \"Amber Horizon\" 208/2010 Universal, Japan (SS 03/2028, DD 03/2026) to Chinese interests at USD 33 mill. Remind you that back in September, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Golden Gayle\" 206/2011 Universal, Japan (SS/DD 12/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 40 mill. The Capesize \"Nordboen Sun\" 169/2010 Daehan, Korea (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 23,5 mill. For reference, the two-years-older \"Genco Hadrian\" 169/2008 Sungdong, Korea (SS 12/2028, DD 11/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold back in July at USD 25 mill. Anglo-Eastern committed their Post Panamax \"Pisces First\" 93/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 12/2025, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at high USD 12 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Potina\" 93/2011 Jiangsu, China (SS 02/2026, DD 12/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at high USD 13 mill. On the Kamsarmax sector, Arcelormittal Shipping committer their \"AM Contrecoeur\" 82/2011 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS/DD 11/2026, BWTS fitted) at low-mid USD 17 mill. Remind you that back in October, the one- year-older \"PS Cadiz\" 82/2010 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 16,8 mill. Furthermore, the \"Yangze 12\" 81/2019 Jiangsu, China (SS 01/2029, DD 11/2026, BWTS fitted) was committed at excess USD 29 mill, while the one-year-younger \"Vincent Triton\" 81/2020 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in September at USD 29,95 mill. Three 2009-built Supramax vessels were committed this week. The \"Aurora SB\" 56/2009 Mitsui, Japan (SS 09/2029, DD 10/2027, BWTS fitted) was committed at mid-high USD 15 mill, while the sister vessel \"Atlantica Sun\" 55/2009 Mitsui, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 15,2 mill. In addition, the \"PPS Luck\" 55/2009 Kawasaki, Japan (SS 01/2029, DD 02/2027, BWTS fitted) was committed at mid-high USD 15 mill.",
    "tankers": "MM Marine committed their Suezmax \"Umnenga II\" 162/2006 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 04/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted, Ice Class 1A, CPP) at USD 36 mill. For reference, the one-year-older \"Seoul Spirit\" 160/2005 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 10/2025) was sold back in June at USD 34,5 mill. The Aframax \"Sofia II\" 105/2008 Sumitomo, Japan (SS 09/2028, DD 12/2026, BWTS fitted) of Flynn Ventures was committed at low USD 30's mill. Remind you that a month ago, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Serene Sea\" 105/2009 Sumitomo, Japan (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 36,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low usd 10,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 9,000/12,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 7,000/10,000 pd. Indonesian and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 9,000/12,000 pd. Indian trips via East Africa into China were reported at the level of usd 8,000/10,000 pd. South African trips into India were fixed around usd 10,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 275K. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips were fixed around usd 10,000/11,000 pd. US Gulf trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K/500K. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 12,000/13,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 200K/300K. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 200K/400K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Trips from China into India were reported at the level of usd 10,000/13,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. South African trips into China were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 160K/180K. South African trips into India were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 140K/160K. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 100K/300K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 12,000/14,000 pd. West African trips into South America were fixed around usd 6,000/8,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. South American trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
